      "message": "Are there any cases we would be validating something that is passed in as a kwarg explicitly?\n\nIf so this will not work as it\u0027ll raise a key error.\n\nSuggest wrapping in an if statement:\n    if resource_to_validate in kwargs:\n        schema_validator.validate(kwargs[resource_to_validate])\n\nAlternatively, making the error / exception a bit more explicit (code wont actually work):\n    try:\n        schema_validator.validate(kwargs[resource_to_validate])\n    except KeyError:\n        raise Exception(\u0027expected \u003cresource to validate\u003e argument in call to func.__name__, argument not found\u0027)\n\nJust trying to avoid an exception that runs back to the decorator that is harder to follow back in an edge case.",
